    "description": "Our trouser shortening service is designed to provide customers with the perfect fit for their trousers. Prices vary based on the type of the trouser as they require different type of handling - for example tailored trousers have blind stitches and often tapes inside, while stonewashed jeans require shortening method that keep the original look.\nYou don’t have to mark you alterations if you come to studio; a member of our team can assist you.\nPostal: To ensure the best results, we ask that customers provide us with a clean garment, and mark or fold the desired length themselves before shipping it or provide a similar fit reference garment.\n- Please ensure to check our \"before sending guide\" for instructions on how to properly prepare your trousers for alteration.- If you are unsure about how to mark or fold the desired length, we offer the option to book a technician visit, get in touch with our team, or visit our studio if you are local.- Please note that while we will do our best to maintain the original finish of the trousers. We will inform you if that is not possible. - If your trousers are made from a unique fabric or have trimmings, there may be an extra handling charge. Please contact us if you are unsure about this before shipping your trousers.\nPlease also note that there are some risks associated with marking or folding the desired length incorrectly. We recommend that customers take care when marking or folding the desired length, as we cannot be held responsible for any damages that may occur if the trousers are marked or folded incorrectly. If you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to reach out to our team.",

